    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d989">

                <pb facs="0869" n="753" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg753"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/3087a.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the American Minister to Cuba
                    </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d989-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-03-20T18:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 20, 1912—6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>After the words “but merely,” last sentence first paragraph, of Department’s
                    March 6, 7 p.m., insert the words “to prevent smuggling and any other
                    infractions of our so-called neutrality statutes and.”</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Huntington Wilson.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d989-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d989-f1-content">
                <p>Same to all Latin-American missions.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
